And Brother Matthew was doing so well. AC of -20, fireproof speed
boots, casting magic missile and Identify at 0% failure with a robe.

Alas, I was missing levitation, which meant Medusa's Isle had to wait.
Naturally,I thought, I'll take the castle, get the WoW and there's my
RoL. I didn't have reflection yet (no wand of polymorph and no luck
with random amulets. Sokoban gave me a second BoH), so I resorted to a
SoR that I found on the dungeon floor. It didn't make me happy, since
it made my blows less effective and really hurt spellcasting. But I
was afraid one of the soldiers might have a wand of death, so on it
went.

I dug down from Medusa's isle, and ended up on what I assume is the
replacement for Gehennom's mazes. Very cool -- essentially a gnomish
mine level with a river of lava running through it. Had to use scare
monster, as I got ganged up on my a Gold Dragon, an Ettin (does
Sporkhack ramp up the wallop for these?) and assorted other nasties.
Cleared it out, and descended to the castle.

I'd planned to find the passtune with my harp by playing MasterMind,
but that didn't seem to work. Is this taken out of Sporkhack? I've not
used it before, so perhaps I wasn't standing in the right place?

Using my Amulet of ESP, I surveyed the situation. Lots of liches, so I
thought it might be time to use my blessed scroll of genocide. Alas,
genociding Ls only took out master and demiliches, leaving plenty of
archliches to counter. At least I wouldn't have to worry about the
touch of death (no MR).

I opened the drawbridge with a wand of opening and started to take
care of business, getting zapped occasionally to little effect by
wands from the soldiers on the ramparts.

A soldier destroyed the drawbridge with a wand of striking, but since
I had a wand of cold, I wasn't worried. So I was pleasantly taking out
nasties as they arrived, when an archlich drank a potion of gain
level. Ha! He disintegrated as soon as he became a Master Lich.

Then, another archlich cast summon nasties, surrounding me. This was a
problem, but not huge. I dropped a scroll of scare monster and was
holding my own ... until a magic eye cast "slow" on me. Crap. Hadn't
expected that. Things were starting to look bad, so I got out my
cursed potion of gain level ... and the damned magic eye attached me
with a fiery gaze, blowing it up. Ugh. Time to dig down, then ... but
before I could do so a purple worm resisted the scroll of scare
monster and consumed me. First digestion took 35 HP. Dug down, was
expelled ... and then promptly engulfed again, taking the rest of my
HP.

So far, very fun ... but much tougher than vanilla, no doubt.


